52 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 40 0 R
/E (To explore deep learning techniques applied to medical image analysis and semantic segmentation. To construct and load a trained U-Net neural network architecture within the PyTorch framework. To design an end-to-end data preprocessing pipeline for standardizing input MRI brain slices.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
53 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 40 0 R
/E (To generate continuous abnormality probability heatmaps and derive binary segmentation masks. To visualize predictions using Matplotlib and construct clear visual overlays onto original images. To export high-resolution segmentation masks and quantitative evaluation visual outputs.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
54 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 40 0 R
/E (Brain tumors represent one of the most severe and life-threatening medical conditions, necessitating precise diagnostic evaluation. Magnetic Resonance Imaging \(MRI\) is widely utilized to examine brain tissues and identify structural abnormalities. In this project, I implemented an automated brain MRI abnormality segmentation pipeline leveraging a deep learning model based on the U-Net architecture.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
55 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 40 0 R
/E (The system accepts a compatible multi-channel MRI slice, performs standard image preprocessing and channel- wise normalization, and processes the tensor through the convolutional network. The model computes a continuous probability map indicating region abnormalities, which is subsequently converted into a binary segmentation mask using thresholding. The results are rendered and visual overlays are generated for spatial verification.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
56 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 40 0 R
/E (Medical image segmentation involves partitioning a digital image into meaningful anatomical regions to isolate structures of interest. In neuro-oncology, standard manual segmentation of brain MRI scans is time-consuming and subject to inter-observer variability. Deep learning models, specifically Convolutional Neural Networks \(CNNs\), have significantly improved automated semantic segmentation tasks.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
57 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 40 0 R
/E (The U-Net architecture is specifically engineered for biomedical image segmentation, featuring a symmetric encoder-decoder structure with skip connections that preserve spatial granularity across resolution scales. This project documents my practical implementation of a U-Net segmentation workflow using PyTorch, demonstrating effective pixel-wise classification on brain MRI datasets.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
